Well, I managed to get uudecode to work on the posted hack archives
and I have the archives in my directory.  Now I download the arc files
to my mac and then port 'em over to an IBM (through TOPS).  Great, I
have two archives on one IBM harddrive.  I start to dearchive nhack23e
and find what?  Bunches and bunches of 'Warning: <file> failed CRC
check' warnings.  I try an 'arc t nhack23e' and it seems to check out
ok.  Still, when I look at the 'leftovers' of the dearching I find
documents that are missing such things as carrage returns and all
sorts of nifty and screwy things.

If I try to unarchive nhexe23e, it seems to work fine for a while and
then nothing.  The computer just hangs and I sit around feeling very
foolish and stupid (%$@% IBMs!)  I've had enough.  I want nethack for
my Macintosh!  (I'd like it on the IBM as well but, well, can't get
the durned thing to work.)  If someone has a working NH2.3 on the IBM,
and a Macintosh that they can port it over to, I'd appreciate if they
move the program and support files to the macintosh, archive it with
StuffIt, BINHEX it, and mail the whole durned thing to me.

On the other hand, if someone can get to handies.ucar.edu
(128.117.64.4) I'd appreciate if they could send me the nethack for
the macintosh on that machine.  (I can't seem to ftp to it myself)

What I'd really like (of course) is the source code for the macintosh
version.  Anyone, anyone?

	Thanx in advance		-Kelesi

